Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||11-29-2001||04:35 PM||||Ok, so I'm not usually jealous of movie/tv star type people.  But I was watching the Tonight show with Jay Leno on Tuesday night- his guest: Frankie Muniz of "Malcom in the Middle" they started discussing his purchase of his first car...  <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/malcolm.jpg">   <BR>Frankie is 15 (turning 16 next week) and recently bought his first car:<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ffjetta.jpg">   <BR>The VW Jetta III from "The Fast & The Furious"!<P>Now when the discussion started- I expected him to be spending a pretty penny on a Caddy, Mercedes, BMW or the likes.  But that Jetta sold on Ebay for nearly $100k!  My first car (an '84 Fiero SE) ran me a steep $750, had to be pull started to get home, and had nothing left of the throwout bearing.  I invested at least $1700 into the car and just sold it (to lowfierogt) for $250!<P>I guess I'm just feeling a little jealous that the kid got to spend $100k on his first car.  Like I said, I don't usually feel jeaolus towards movie/tv people (Nichols Cage can buy, sell, race (and crash) as many Ferraris as he wants...) It just seemed different this time.<P>[/rant]<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">   <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||frontal lobe||11-29-2001||05:25 PM||||I first thought it was going to be one of those electric jeeps like you get at Toys-r-us!<P>He spends that much on a car!  He should be saving that money up for therapy for a couple years from now when the show goes off the air and he is unemployed at age 18, and a has-been.  Ever heard of Danny Bonaduce?<P>Not wishing it on him.  He seems like a decent kid.||||reg||1
