Z||000026||MinnGreenGT||12-04-2001||10:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>The car probably has no more HP than what it came with from VW. It was a prop-car. Why would a movie build up a VW thats in one scene? It was built just for looks<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually as Slammed Fiero mentioned above, the car was built before the movie- not for the movie!  So it was built for some extra power (wish I still had the specs on it... next month when the movie comes out I'm sure they'll be available).<P>Anyway, there were at least 3 of each car built, usually one for close-ups (this was the <B>real</B> car for each), and 2 for driving/stunts/destruction.<P>Although I don't approve of the car overall- a VW is far from the worst vehicle he could've bought... they <B>can</B> be made to go quite well.  Think about it, our cars are made to cruise on Highways with 70mph speed limits.  VWs are built for the autobahn- have you ever been on the autobahn? I have... and you better be flyin' well above 100mph if you want to spend any time in the left lane without a BMW or Mercedes up your tailpipe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
